    <string name="guide_title">How to connect</string>
    <string name="guide_body">ON THIS PHONE (native)\n\n1. Tap \"Install agy\". The app downloads Google\'s official Android build of the Antigravity CLI and checks its SHA-512 checksum.\n2. Tap \"Start Antigravity\". agy starts in the built-in terminal in ~/projects.\n3. Sign in: agy opens Google sign-in in Chrome. After you approve, Chrome returns to agy automatically. If nothing opens, tap \"Open\" on the blue banner.\n4. Agents keep running in the background (see the notification). Use the menu for more sessions or a plain shell.\n\nNeeds a 64-bit ARM phone. The desktop editor (GUI) does not run on Android, only the agent CLI.\n\nOPTION 1: Official Remote Control (recommended)\n\n1. On your computer, open Antigravity → Settings (Ctrl+, / Cmd+,).\n2. Turn on \"Enable Remote Control\" (Application or Account section, depending on the version). In the CLI: agy --remote-control, or /remote-control inside a session.\n3. Keep the computer awake and Antigravity open.\n4. In this app tap \"Antigravity Remote Control (official)\" and sign in with the SAME Google account.\n5. Pick your computer in the instance switcher.\n\nTip: When Antigravity shows an \"Open in Remote Control\" QR code, scan it with the phone camera. The link opens in this app.\n\nIf Google refuses to sign in inside the app, use the \"Chrome\" button. Sign-in inside Chrome always works.\n\nOPTION 2: Your own bridge\nAny web address that exposes your computer works: code-server, a noVNC remote desktop, an open-source Antigravity mobile bridge, or a Cloudflare / Tailscale tunnel. Tap \"Add connection\" and enter its address.\n\nWith Remote Control the agents run on your computer.</string>
